      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Violence** (2005) represents a pivotal moment in Mexican cinema's exploration of urban brutality. Director Luis Mandoki crafts a raw, unflinching look at Mexico City's criminal underbelly that shares DNA with **Amores Perros** (2000) and **City of God** (2002). The film's visceral approach to depicting street violence influenced later works like <a href=\"/movie/77635\" class=\"movie-title\">Miss Bala</a> (2011) and **Heli** (2013), establishing a new visual language for Latin American crime dramas."
